From 25329fc3e5f92db050dd16401996b4d33b2fa338 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri Geelen <dimitri@geelenandcompany.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:39:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Stray screen-capture detector and audit rail (from 832
 T-936; AEF T-3572)

tools/_t936-stray-capture-scan.py finds ImageMagick import(1) output by its PostScript header,
not by filename (none of 832's four captures had an extension), over the repo root and working
directories; --facts gives count, bytes, largest canvas and paths. The audit rail WARNs and names
the files; whether to look at or delete them is the operator's call (they are images of the
operator's screen). This covers what the PreToolUse gate cannot: leaks inside a running shell.
Teeth: tools/_t936-capture-scan-teeth.sh.
---
